Revision history for Web-Route

0.01  unreleased
    - First version: Flask-like routes as plain functions in the route:: package (route::get, post, put,
      patch, delete, head, options, any, add, list, clear; :name and *name parameters; nothing exported that
      clashes), requests as plain hashes, responses as [status, headers, body] (a hash becomes JSON,
      a string text), json / text / stream / sse helpers, and a small sequential HTTP/1.1 server on a unix
      socket (or host:port) for behind nginx: streamed responses, client-gone detection, limits, SIGTERM.
    - pull responses: bodies the server pulls while serving other connections (non-blocking writes), with a
      tick hook per round and on_close for clients that leave early: many slow responses at once.
